/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Humidification means adding water vapour to air.
   - Spray chamber or air washer.
   - Wetted-surface humidifier.
   - Steam injection.
   - In spray chambers and wetted-surface humidifiers the driving force is the difference between the vapour pressure at the water surface and the partial pressure of water vapour in the air.
   - Dehumidification means removing water vapour.
   - Cooling below the dew point.
   - Liquid absorption.
   - Solid adsorption.
   - Compression.
*/
