/* book exam traps: Setting X* = 0. At any relative humidity a hygroscopic solid has X* > 0; air cannot dry it to zero. | Swapping bases. A 30 % wet-basis sample has X = 0.429, not 0.30. | Using X − X* when X is on a wet basis. Convert both moisture contents to dry basis first. | Confusing free moisture with unbound moisture. Free is above equilibrium; unbound is pore water. | Using a room-temperature isotherm for a hot dryer. X* falls as temperature rises, and hysteresis matters. */
